# E §5 step 1 (tally 2.1.2, issue #34, the user's "1: refused stays refused", 2026-11-03): zero (known 2026-02-01)
# makes rent[2026-03]'s amount refused at its booking cut (0 tenants, RUN-DIV). A booking refused at κ₀ stays refused,
# and its later re-measurements record nothing, as a hole booking's refused steps: late1 (4 tenants) and late2
# (5 tenants) make no adjustment (n), July's flows of rent stand (q), and konto stays refused from March 10 (b).
# tally 2.1.1's refcore skipped late1's step and measured late2's against it: one adjustment of -50.00 PLN dated
# 2026-07-01, unsettled, so q was the HOLE-CHANGED hole; the literal "refusal spreads" would refuse two adjustments.
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
source act "act"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input total: money PLN
input tenants[m in months]: int
input dom: int

move rent[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to landlord amount round(total / tenants[m], minor(PLN), half-even)

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  total = 1 000.00 PLN "umowa"
  dom = 10 "umowa"
  tenants[*] = 2 "umowa"
  opening[konto] = 10 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

version zero
  cite act
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-02-01
  replace tenants[*] = 0 "aneks 1"

version late1
  cite act
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-05-01
  replace tenants[*] = 4 "aneks 2"

version late2
  cite act
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-07-01
  replace tenants[*] = 5 "aneks 3"

ask n: count(x in adjustments over 2026)
ask q: flows(rent, 2026-07-01 .. 2026-07-31)
ask b: bal(konto, 2026-02-28), bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
=== expect
b: (9 000.00 PLN, refused: RUN-DIV division by zero)
  unfulfilled: rent[2026-01]
  unfulfilled: rent[2026-02]
  cut 2026-10-20
n: 0
  cut 2026-10-20
q: 500.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: rent[2026-07]
  cut 2026-10-20
